Special Topics:

  - Time Elapsed: currently we grab the current time at the beginning of the game, storing the timestamp in a timespec struct in board, we then calculate the difference between now and that time,
  - Ticker & Time Elapsed: currently the ticker is only used for ball movement, though we could perform a tick on 1second intervals, incrementing the ticker, and calculating the difference that way,
  - Accuracy: this was one of the areas where it made sense to work with the timespec struct, as we are working with a modular example of a structure of time, not coupled to anything else,
  - Efficiency: there are a very small amount (5 specifically) of system calls in the whole project, which are associated primarily with the ticker and ball movement.

